# Defense-in-depth npm pack exclusions.
# The primary mechanism is the `files` allowlist in package.json.
# Anything matched here that is NOT matched by the allowlist is excluded.
# Anything matched by BOTH means it stays in the tarball.
#
# The `files` allowlist intentionally uses file-extension globs
# (e.g. dist/**/*.js) instead of whole directories. That alone
# keeps stray .log / .ndjson / .pid sentinels out of the package.

/src/
/tests/
/vendor/
/coverage/
/.git/
/.github/
/.gitignore
/.npmignore

/docs/

/scripts/

/emotes/_unused/
/emotes/ascii-bear/
/emotes/aza_choi/
/emotes/aza_choi_nobg/
/emotes/test/

/.tmp/
**/*.tmp
**/*.bak
**/rescue-*
**/*-rescue-*